WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.619 --> 00:00:01.721
- There's so many people that you see

00:00:01.721 --> 00:00:03.489
that are in this industry
or just life in general

00:00:03.489 --> 00:00:04.829
that are going through their days

00:00:04.829 --> 00:00:07.573
and may have everything
they could ever want

00:00:07.573 --> 00:00:09.044
but they're not happy.

00:00:09.044 --> 00:00:10.667
Confidence is the best, I think.

00:00:10.667 --> 00:00:14.085
You could literally rock a trash
bag if you have confidence.

00:00:14.085 --> 00:00:15.878
I don't need to cuss and whatever.

00:00:15.878 --> 00:00:17.793
I don't need to do that
to make a great song.

00:00:17.793 --> 00:00:19.027
Michael Jackson never did it,

00:00:19.027 --> 00:00:21.368
so I don't think I got to
do it either, you know?

00:00:21.368 --> 00:00:24.433
- She's an American
actress, singer, and dancer.

00:00:24.433 --> 00:00:26.647
In March 2016 she was cast in

00:00:26.647 --> 00:00:29.596
the Spider-Man film
Homecoming as Michelle.

00:00:29.596 --> 00:00:31.260
She began her professional career as

00:00:31.260 --> 00:00:33.988
a fashion model for Old Navy and Macy's.

00:00:33.988 --> 00:00:35.392
She's Zendaya and here's my take

00:00:35.392 --> 00:00:37.897
on her top 10 rules for success.

00:00:37.897 --> 00:00:39.399
Rule number one is my personal favorite

00:00:39.399 --> 00:00:41.021
and make sure to stick
around all the way to the end

00:00:41.021 --> 00:00:42.568
for some special bonus clips.

00:00:42.568 --> 00:00:44.157
Also as she's talking
if she says something

00:00:44.157 --> 00:00:46.008
that really resonates with you,

00:00:46.008 --> 00:00:47.119
please leave it in the comments below,

00:00:47.119 --> 00:00:48.142
put quotes around it,

00:00:48.142 --> 00:00:50.499
so other people can be inspired as well.

00:00:50.499 --> 00:00:51.332
Enjoy.

00:00:55.076 --> 00:00:58.576
(intense uplifting music)

00:01:04.456 --> 00:01:06.408
- What's your message
for viewers out there

00:01:06.408 --> 00:01:07.706
about following your dreams?

00:01:07.706 --> 00:01:08.789
- I would say

00:01:10.033 --> 00:01:11.622
if you truly believe in something

00:01:11.622 --> 00:01:13.243
and you really have a
passion for something,

00:01:13.243 --> 00:01:14.859
then go for it.

00:01:14.859 --> 00:01:16.288
I think there's a lot of obstacles

00:01:16.288 --> 00:01:18.368
that you have to go
through and nothing's ever

00:01:18.368 --> 00:01:21.822
given to you and it takes a lot
of hard work and dedication,

00:01:21.822 --> 00:01:24.324
but if you really believe in
it, then you should do it.

00:01:24.324 --> 00:01:26.530
Confidence is the best, I think.

00:01:26.530 --> 00:01:30.420
You can literally rock a trash
bag if you have confidence.

00:01:30.420 --> 00:01:31.356
Literally.

00:01:31.356 --> 00:01:33.289
Lady Gaga does it all the time.

00:01:33.289 --> 00:01:34.435
She can rock whatever she wants

00:01:34.435 --> 00:01:35.476
because she has that confidence

00:01:35.476 --> 00:01:36.826
that makes you believe that it's

00:01:36.826 --> 00:01:38.175
just the coolest thing ever.

00:01:38.175 --> 00:01:39.468
And I think that that's awesome.

00:01:39.468 --> 00:01:41.179
You know, when you see a confident woman,

00:01:41.179 --> 00:01:43.132
I think there's nothing more attractive

00:01:43.132 --> 00:01:45.498
or fabulous about a confident woman

00:01:45.498 --> 00:01:47.007
because you know that she

00:01:47.007 --> 00:01:49.033
loves herself and is in her own skin

00:01:49.033 --> 00:01:51.554
and I think that's the best.

00:01:51.554 --> 00:01:54.678
It's the best accessory,
it's the best outfit,

00:01:54.678 --> 00:01:55.922
it's confidence.

00:01:55.922 --> 00:01:57.794
Well the best thing I've learned

00:01:57.794 --> 00:02:00.176
and advice I could give
maybe my younger self,

00:02:00.176 --> 00:02:01.760
is really to focus on happiness.

00:02:01.760 --> 00:02:03.448
You know, happiness is the key because

00:02:03.448 --> 00:02:05.051
there's so many people that you see

00:02:05.051 --> 00:02:07.058
that are in this industry
or just in life in general

00:02:07.058 --> 00:02:08.130
that are going through their days

00:02:08.130 --> 00:02:11.001
and may have everything
they could ever want,

00:02:11.001 --> 00:02:12.639
but they're not happy, you know?

00:02:12.639 --> 00:02:14.148
So you have to focus
on what makes you happy

00:02:14.148 --> 00:02:17.400
and make decisions in your career,

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:19.479
in your life that make you happy.

00:02:19.479 --> 00:02:21.091
And so I've been trying to do that

00:02:21.091 --> 00:02:22.752
and it's working, you know?

00:02:22.752 --> 00:02:25.534
And saying no to things that are negative

00:02:25.534 --> 00:02:28.525
and saying no to things
that you don't want to do.

00:02:28.525 --> 00:02:29.625
You know?

00:02:29.625 --> 00:02:32.213
So I think that that's my
biggest piece of advice.

00:02:32.213 --> 00:02:34.694
Something I do or I try to do every day,

00:02:34.694 --> 00:02:36.777
is I try to make someone,

00:02:37.817 --> 00:02:40.043
whether it be in my team
or my life or whatever,

00:02:40.043 --> 00:02:40.876
just happy.

00:02:40.876 --> 00:02:44.099
Or I try to make them feel
good or feel comfortable

00:02:44.099 --> 00:02:46.619
or feel loved, whatever it may be.

00:02:46.619 --> 00:02:48.114
It could be the littlest thing,

00:02:48.114 --> 00:02:50.680
it could just be saying, oh
you look really pretty today.

00:02:50.680 --> 00:02:51.930
Or it could be,

00:02:53.083 --> 00:02:54.242
something even smaller than that

00:02:54.242 --> 00:02:56.050
or something bigger than that, you know?

00:02:56.050 --> 00:02:58.452
It doesn't really matter but it's just

00:02:58.452 --> 00:03:00.587
making a conscious effort
to make someone feel good.

00:03:00.587 --> 00:03:02.237
And that could be a stranger

00:03:02.237 --> 00:03:04.210
or it could be your mom, you know?

00:03:04.210 --> 00:03:06.697
I'm not pretending to be
something that I am not

00:03:06.697 --> 00:03:09.486
or pretending to be this
goody two-shoes or whatever,

00:03:09.486 --> 00:03:10.934
I'm just being myself.

00:03:10.934 --> 00:03:12.673
And I think that, you know,

00:03:12.673 --> 00:03:15.054
then nobody can be disappointed
in who I am as a person

00:03:15.054 --> 00:03:17.473
or I don't feel like I
have to hide or pretend

00:03:17.473 --> 00:03:18.731
because I'm not.

00:03:18.731 --> 00:03:20.275
I'm just being Zendaya, you know?

00:03:20.275 --> 00:03:22.877
And I'm just going
through life and learning

00:03:22.877 --> 00:03:24.877
how to be a young woman.

00:03:25.735 --> 00:03:28.454
You know, and I have that responsibility,

00:03:28.454 --> 00:03:29.689
I think it's a responsibility.

00:03:29.689 --> 00:03:31.367
Is it a little bit of a weight sometimes?

00:03:31.367 --> 00:03:33.046
Absolutely but it's a responsibility

00:03:33.046 --> 00:03:34.928
that I'm willing to take.
- I love that.

00:03:34.928 --> 00:03:35.970
- You know if you don't get the part,

00:03:35.970 --> 00:03:38.771
it wasn't yours to begin with.

00:03:38.771 --> 00:03:40.431
And that's the truth,
it wasn't meant for you.

00:03:40.431 --> 00:03:41.848
I feel like if the opportunities

00:03:41.848 --> 00:03:42.859
and what's meant to happen to you

00:03:42.859 --> 00:03:45.278
is going to happen to you and
you just have to trust that,

00:03:45.278 --> 00:03:46.383
and you have to work hard.

00:03:46.383 --> 00:03:47.889
What I did is I just,

00:03:47.889 --> 00:03:50.005
I knew something was going to happen.

00:03:50.005 --> 00:03:52.541
It wasn't a matter of if,
it was a matter of when,

00:03:52.541 --> 00:03:54.609
so I just worked hard until I got there.

00:03:54.609 --> 00:03:56.948
And I had the goal, I knew what I wanted,

00:03:56.948 --> 00:03:58.536
and so when I came into LA,

00:03:58.536 --> 00:04:00.291
things happened a lot faster for me

00:04:00.291 --> 00:04:02.004
because I had my goal, I was ready to go

00:04:02.004 --> 00:04:03.536
and I was a new face.

00:04:03.536 --> 00:04:04.906
- It worked out, right?

00:04:04.906 --> 00:04:05.739
- That's right.

00:04:05.739 --> 00:04:07.246
But of course there was nos,
of course there was nos,

00:04:07.246 --> 00:04:10.016
but at the end of the day my eye was like,

00:04:10.016 --> 00:04:12.046
it's going to happen,
it's going to happen.

00:04:12.046 --> 00:04:13.785
I've been taking a long time to like,

00:04:13.785 --> 00:04:15.815
you know those four years since Replay

00:04:15.815 --> 00:04:16.672
and everything like that.

00:04:16.672 --> 00:04:18.940
Or three years, however long it's been.

00:04:18.940 --> 00:04:21.080
Just taking the time because

00:04:21.080 --> 00:04:23.615
A, I've grown as a woman.

00:04:23.615 --> 00:04:24.448
You know what I mean?

00:04:24.448 --> 00:04:26.527
You learn who you are,
you come into your own,

00:04:26.527 --> 00:04:28.074
you find out more about yourself.

00:04:28.074 --> 00:04:30.364
And that's a big transitional
period, you know what I mean?

00:04:30.364 --> 00:04:34.099
When you're growing into
literally becoming a woman.

00:04:34.099 --> 00:04:36.826
My thing was how I translated that

00:04:36.826 --> 00:04:38.713
and turned that into the music.

00:04:38.713 --> 00:04:39.546
You know what I mean?

00:04:39.546 --> 00:04:41.573
How do I translate my
maturity and my growth

00:04:41.573 --> 00:04:44.211
and let people connect to that

00:04:44.211 --> 00:04:46.270
and make it a little more real?

00:04:46.270 --> 00:04:47.892
Also on the same token,

00:04:47.892 --> 00:04:51.051
you know, I'm finally getting
the chance to really do

00:04:51.051 --> 00:04:53.539
the music that I want to
do, you know what I mean?

00:04:53.539 --> 00:04:56.643
There is no sacrificing anything.

00:04:56.643 --> 00:04:59.088
There's no, you know, giving in.

00:04:59.088 --> 00:05:01.939
You know, people have opinions.

00:05:01.939 --> 00:05:03.565
You know, behind the scenes of like

00:05:03.565 --> 00:05:06.738
what lane I should go in
and what I need to do,

00:05:06.738 --> 00:05:08.142
but I know what I want.

00:05:08.142 --> 00:05:09.428
And that's my number one piece of advice

00:05:09.428 --> 00:05:10.923
for anyone who's doing anything in life,

00:05:10.923 --> 00:05:12.640
is you have to stick to your vision

00:05:12.640 --> 00:05:14.081
and stick to your gut,
you know what I'm saying?

00:05:14.081 --> 00:05:18.413
Olivia Pope gut, go with it,
it works every time, you know?

00:05:18.413 --> 00:05:21.582
Acting, singing, and dancing I think

00:05:21.582 --> 00:05:24.155
are all things that came to me naturally

00:05:24.155 --> 00:05:27.329
but they're all things that
I try to challenge myself on.

00:05:27.329 --> 00:05:28.913
So I'm always trying to push myself

00:05:28.913 --> 00:05:32.033
in every area of the arts whether it be

00:05:32.033 --> 00:05:33.947
acting, singing, or dancing.

00:05:33.947 --> 00:05:36.264
It's about whether it be perfecting

00:05:36.264 --> 00:05:38.132
the dance that you already know,

00:05:38.132 --> 00:05:39.837
or learning a new style of dance.

00:05:39.837 --> 00:05:41.513
Or whether it be trying to hit a note

00:05:41.513 --> 00:05:42.931
that you never thought you could hit

00:05:42.931 --> 00:05:46.739
or play a character that
is outside of your range.

00:05:46.739 --> 00:05:48.716
Then you know, that's something
I want to continue to do

00:05:48.716 --> 00:05:50.611
and continue to grow.

00:05:50.611 --> 00:05:52.681
I think if you stop challenging yourself

00:05:52.681 --> 00:05:55.708
then there's no more, you stop yourself.

00:05:55.708 --> 00:05:58.707
But there's no limit to the
things that you're capable of,

00:05:58.707 --> 00:06:01.481
so I think I'm going to
continue to challenge myself.

00:06:01.481 --> 00:06:03.740
Here's my thing, is I'm always very

00:06:03.740 --> 00:06:06.253
careful about how I do,

00:06:06.253 --> 00:06:08.178
like especially when it
comes to topics on music.

00:06:08.178 --> 00:06:10.129
It's like, you can talk around things,

00:06:10.129 --> 00:06:12.702
I just am not going to
say, you know what I mean?

00:06:12.702 --> 00:06:14.121
You can talk around things, so it's like

00:06:14.121 --> 00:06:15.785
really it can mean
whatever it wants to mean

00:06:15.785 --> 00:06:16.992
for whoever is listening to it.

00:06:16.992 --> 00:06:17.825
You know what I'm saying?

00:06:17.825 --> 00:06:19.879
It's up to you to decide
what that means to you.

00:06:19.879 --> 00:06:22.324
And that's like kind of
how I want to keep it

00:06:22.324 --> 00:06:24.778
and I think that's kind of
like the greatest in the world.

00:06:24.778 --> 00:06:26.965
Like Michael Jackson,
you know what I mean?

00:06:26.965 --> 00:06:28.629
He talked around all kinds of things.

00:06:28.629 --> 00:06:29.810
- Even the song Creep itself,

00:06:29.810 --> 00:06:31.240
like I remember listening to it.

00:06:31.240 --> 00:06:32.843
- Have no idea what it means.

00:06:32.843 --> 00:06:34.671
- Literally like somebody creeping like.

00:06:34.671 --> 00:06:35.504
- [Zendaya] Exactly.

00:06:35.504 --> 00:06:36.715
- But it's what you put into it as well.

00:06:36.715 --> 00:06:38.429
- Exactly, it's what you want to make it

00:06:38.429 --> 00:06:39.643
and I think that that's the way,

00:06:39.643 --> 00:06:40.797
that's kind of like the loophole.

00:06:40.797 --> 00:06:42.137
That's the way to have edgy music

00:06:42.137 --> 00:06:44.008
and allow my older fan base or whatever

00:06:44.008 --> 00:06:46.076
to enjoy the music and understand it

00:06:46.076 --> 00:06:47.631
and also have young people listen to it

00:06:47.631 --> 00:06:50.024
because it doesn't have to be.

00:06:50.024 --> 00:06:51.770
And I don't need to cuss and whatever,

00:06:51.770 --> 00:06:53.694
I don't need to do that
to make a great song.

00:06:53.694 --> 00:06:54.968
Michael Jackson never did it,

00:06:54.968 --> 00:06:57.677
so I don't think I got to
do it either, you know?

00:06:57.677 --> 00:06:59.479
So it's just, I think,

00:06:59.479 --> 00:07:01.909
it's a balance, you know what I'm saying?

00:07:01.909 --> 00:07:03.652
It's a way to be edgy and push the limits

00:07:03.652 --> 00:07:06.120
but do it at the right pace.

00:07:06.120 --> 00:07:07.602
This whole kind of transition

00:07:07.602 --> 00:07:09.255
into womanhood is all about pace,

00:07:09.255 --> 00:07:11.486
taking my time, making the right steps

00:07:11.486 --> 00:07:13.685
and the right moves when it
needs to be made, you know?

00:07:13.685 --> 00:07:15.090
Not going too fast.

00:07:15.090 --> 00:07:18.469
I have decided that I want
to do what makes me happy

00:07:18.469 --> 00:07:20.575
for as long as it makes me happy.

00:07:20.575 --> 00:07:22.216
So if that means, and this is something

00:07:22.216 --> 00:07:23.295
my parents have always told me,

00:07:23.295 --> 00:07:25.910
if that means I wake up
tomorrow and I decide that

00:07:25.910 --> 00:07:28.653
none of this is making me
happy, it's not fulfilling me,

00:07:28.653 --> 00:07:30.936
it's making me a miserable
person, I don't feel good.

00:07:30.936 --> 00:07:32.586
- What are you going to go do?

00:07:32.586 --> 00:07:33.419
- Something else.

00:07:33.419 --> 00:07:34.710
- What?
- I don't know.

00:07:34.710 --> 00:07:35.543
- But like what?

00:07:35.543 --> 00:07:36.501
- We'll decide when we get there.

00:07:36.501 --> 00:07:37.334
- You've never thought about it?

00:07:37.334 --> 00:07:38.267
Like what else you would do?

00:07:38.267 --> 00:07:41.618
- I would want to like, I would
probably want to go to school,

00:07:41.618 --> 00:07:43.372
I want to go to college.

00:07:43.372 --> 00:07:47.795
Probably for, like, child
psychology, something unrelated.

00:07:47.795 --> 00:07:49.043
Who knows, I might wake up and say,

00:07:49.043 --> 00:07:49.876
you know what?

00:07:49.876 --> 00:07:50.709
I want to be a doctor.

00:07:50.709 --> 00:07:51.542
You know what?

00:07:51.542 --> 00:07:52.656
I want to be a this, I want to be that,

00:07:52.656 --> 00:07:53.775
I don't know what the future holds.

00:07:53.775 --> 00:07:54.753
As long as it makes me happy.

00:07:54.753 --> 00:07:56.085
I got to find a passion, you know?

00:07:56.085 --> 00:07:58.130
But for now, this is making me happy,

00:07:58.130 --> 00:07:59.522
and I'm going to keep doing this.

00:07:59.522 --> 00:08:01.356
Especially if you're
young in this industry,

00:08:01.356 --> 00:08:02.722
you get doubted

00:08:02.722 --> 00:08:04.435
and people like to not listen to you.

00:08:04.435 --> 00:08:05.268
- [Ross] Yeah.

00:08:05.268 --> 00:08:08.073
- And so I'm not one of those
people that cannot be heard.

00:08:08.073 --> 00:08:09.144
You know what I'm saying?

00:08:09.144 --> 00:08:10.925
You know, I think it's very important

00:08:10.925 --> 00:08:13.849
that people exercise their

00:08:13.849 --> 00:08:15.731
voice and what they feel is right

00:08:15.731 --> 00:08:16.902
in your gut and your instinct,

00:08:16.902 --> 00:08:19.245
especially if you're in this
industry as a young person,

00:08:19.245 --> 00:08:20.736
you have to follow your heart

00:08:20.736 --> 00:08:23.319
and do what you think is right.

00:08:24.780 --> 00:08:26.457
