that we forget to use
it for a positive thing,

00:09:23.327 --> 00:09:24.160
you know what I mean?

00:09:24.160 --> 00:09:25.473
Like when I use my Twitter

00:09:25.473 --> 00:09:27.135
to say anything or to do anything,

00:09:27.135 --> 00:09:29.466
I'd use it to make messages
that I think are important

00:09:29.466 --> 00:09:31.975
or to get out things that I
think will make people laugh

00:09:31.975 --> 00:09:33.692
or funny, you know what I mean?

00:09:33.692 --> 00:09:36.371
You know, I'm not going to
tweet something negative

00:09:36.371 --> 00:09:37.258
or hurt somebody's feelings,

00:09:37.258 --> 00:09:38.910
that's just not who I
am, you know what I mean?

00:09:38.910 --> 00:09:41.379
And sometimes we get
so wrapped up in like,

00:09:41.379 --> 00:09:43.748
oh it's funny or oh this is how I feel.

00:09:43.748 --> 00:09:45.841
And you know you're allowed
to express how you feel

00:09:45.841 --> 00:09:48.170
but at the end of the day
we're all human beings.

00:09:48.170 --> 00:09:50.755
Like gosh, you know, we all have feelings

00:09:50.755 --> 00:09:52.858
but you have to be loving of yourself

00:09:52.858 --> 00:09:54.471
and get in touch with yourself

00:09:54.471 --> 00:09:56.407
and be happy with yourself first.

00:09:56.407 --> 00:09:57.833
I think it's less about other people

00:09:57.833 --> 00:09:59.703
and more about like I have
to do better than myself.

00:09:59.703 --> 00:10:01.263
Like if I feel like I reach a level,

00:10:01.263 --> 00:10:02.229
then I have to work harder.

00:10:02.229 --> 00:10:05.361
You're never, you know, the best,

00:10:05.361 --> 00:10:06.961
you can always get better.

00:10:06.961 --> 00:10:08.210
There's always room for improvement

00:10:08.210 --> 00:10:09.276
and that's in every area,

00:10:09.276 --> 00:10:11.602
that's not just as, you
know, an artist or whatever

00:10:11.602 --> 00:10:12.994
but that's just as a human being.

00:10:12.994 --> 00:10:16.997
I constantly try to become a
better person, like I'm like,

00:10:16.997 --> 00:10:19.295
even if I like let negative
thoughts come in my mind

00:10:19.295 --> 00:10:21.383
or I think some type of
way or I'm thinking petty,

00:10:21.383 --> 00:10:23.231
I'm just like, dude, like,
you're better than that.

00:10:23.231 --> 00:10:24.419
You're like zen, chill.

00:10:24.419 --> 00:10:26.302
Like, I'm good, you know what I mean?

00:10:26.302 --> 00:10:29.638
Me, I've been making children's
programming for a long time

00:10:29.638 --> 00:10:31.464
and for me, a lot of people ask me like,

00:10:31.464 --> 00:10:32.618
why are you still on Disney channel?

00:10:32.618 --> 00:10:33.648
Why do you still do that?

00:10:33.648 --> 00:10:37.014
And to me it's because I
still have a responsibility

00:10:37.014 --> 00:10:38.637
as this young person that I am

00:10:38.637 --> 00:10:41.863
to create positive programming
for these young people.

00:10:41.863 --> 00:10:43.436
I have little kids that look up to me

00:10:43.436 --> 00:10:45.398
and I think of that as a responsibility.

00:10:45.398 --> 00:10:47.243
And I know there's so many
parents that come up to me

00:10:47.243 --> 00:10:49.155
and just hearing them say thank you

00:10:49.155 --> 00:10:50.964
for being that for my
daughter or for my son,

00:10:50.964 --> 00:10:52.652
being that inspiration for them,

00:10:52.652 --> 00:10:53.963
that's everything to me.

